{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788304325,"nonce":"oh4+Xp/Eh9xaxQ6nldDfT3/hsCI=","title":"work-cover's clean dry run says 'the journal writer is closed' when it is open and nothing was mutated","message":"A clean `work-cover {dry_run:true}` writes no journal line — correctly — and then reports it in the words of a FAILURE. `data.action` is `{\"journal_seq\": 0, \"provenance\": \"NOT WRITTEN — the journal writer is closed, so this mutation has no journal line. Treat anything done in this session as unprovenanced.\"}`\n\n**Neither clause is true.** The writer is open, and there was no mutation to journal.\n\n## The measurement\n\nBanked bench envelope `accept/runs/s21-20260901/12-workcover-dryrun.json`, s21 orchestrator smoke, assembly `1.0.0+52606d1`. Reported as FINDING 5.2c by `accept/61794cd-bleed-triage.py` on its first live run (290 PASS / 4 FAIL, 2026-09-01) and re-asserted offline at check 9.6w so it cannot be argued away without a bench.\n\n## The mechanism\n\n`PawnManageVerbs.WorkCover`'s emit guard:\n\n    long seq = (repaired.Count \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !dryRun) || stillUnder.Count \u003e 0\n        ? Act(V, dryRun ? \"plan\" : \"cover\", …)\n        : 0;\n    …\n    [\"action\"] = Stamp(seq),\n\nA dry run that plans a COMPLETE repair has `repaired.Count \u003e 0` and `stillUnder.Count == 0`, so both clauses are false, nothing is emitted, and `seq` is 0. `PawnActs.Stamp(0)` then attaches the \"writer is closed\" sentence, because for every other caller `seq == 0` really does mean the emit failed.\n\n`PawnActs.NoStamp()` is the shape this case wants and already exists three lines below `Stamp`: `{\"journal_seq\": null, \"provenance\": \"not applicable — nothing was mutated\"}`. `triage` already uses it for exactly this reason (\"Present and null, so a caller can prove the verb mutated nothing rather than infer it\").\n\n## Why it matters rather than being cosmetic\n\nThe sentence tells an agent to **\"treat anything done in this session as unprovenanced\"** — an instruction to distrust its own ledger, emitted by the one call in the surface that is *guaranteed* to have changed nothing. An agent that believes it has lost journal provenance has no correct next move, and the M1 post-mortem's whole subject is a run that could not tell what it had done.\n\nIt is also the difference `journal_seq: 0` cannot express: 0 currently means both \"the writer is closed\" and \"no row was owed\", which is the absent-vs-null conflation `61794cd` ruled against for `ticks_until_bleedout` and session 21 fixed for `enabled_but_incapable`.\n\n## Fix\n\nDecide from the GUARD, not from the returned seq — `Journal.Emit` can legitimately return 0 when the writer really is closed, and that case must keep its warning:\n\n    bool owed = (repaired.Count \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !dryRun) || stillUnder.Count \u003e 0;\n    long seq = owed ? Act(…) : 0;\n    …\n    [\"action\"] = owed ? Stamp(seq) : NoStamp(),\n\n## Side note, in the same guard\n\nThe `\"plan\"` step name is unreachable except on a dry run that FAILED to fully repair: the only way a dry run emits at all is `stillUnder.Count \u003e 0`. Not a defect, but worth knowing before anyone greps the journal for `step:\"plan\"` expecting every dry run.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `work-cover {work:\"Doctor\", dry_run:true}` on a colony whose Doctor floor is repairable by one promotion publishes `data.action.journal_seq: null`, not `0`.\n- …and a `provenance` sentence that says nothing was mutated — it must not contain the words \"writer is closed\".\n- The journal genuinely carries no `action` row for that call (read the ledger, not the verb's own stamp).\n- A `work-cover` call that DOES emit still publishes an integer `journal_seq` that joins to the ledger row — the existing 5.3e/5.4d behaviour is unchanged.\n- A real `Journal.Emit` failure still produces `Stamp(0)`'s warning: the discriminator is the emit GUARD, not the returned seq.\n- `accept/61794cd-bleed-triage.py`'s FINDING 5.2c becomes a check, and 9.6w's banked assertion is updated or dropped with a note saying why.","files":null}]}